      "published": "01 Jan 2010, 00:00",
      "summary": "Gordon Lightfoot was a Canadian singer-songwriter, born on 17 November 1938 in Orillia, Ontario, who died on 1 May 2023 at the age of 84. He is credited with helping to define the singer-songwriter era of the 1970s, and is counted among Canada&#39;s most influential songwriters. His biographer Nicholas Jennings summed up his subjects as trains, shipwrecks, rivers, highways, lovers &amp; loneliness. Sundown, released in 1974, was his only number one on the US Hot 100. <a href=\"https://www.last.fm/music/Gordon+Lightfoot\">Read more on Last.fm</a>",
